[Host] That's all for today. Japan's parliament has revised the Imperial House Law for the first time in about eighty years, aiming to secure the number of imperial family members. Female members may now stay after marriage, and male-line descendants of former imperial families may be adopted. The law takes effect three months after promulgation and will be reviewed every thirty years. Thanks for listening, and see you tomorrow.

